 point update after it\nhad detected a switch to a different reference.  This could lead\nto an out-of-bounds read because it did not switch to the correct\nintervals array for the later references.  The end values looked\nup in that case were not used, but it could cause a segfault\nif the later references had many more intervals requested than\nthe first one.  Fix by only updating end when on the correct\nreference.\n\nThis bug is present in releases 1.11 to 1.20\")\n\nShow description for 356bfd6 \n\n[ daviesrob ](/samtools/htslib/commits?author=daviesrob)\n\nauthored and \n\n[ jkbonfield ](/samtools/htslib/commits?author=jkbonfield)\n\ncommitted  on Jun 6, 2024 \n\n[ 356bfd6  ](/samtools/htslib/commit/356bfd6b9a573afeed5e4e266f9e15ad71f10896)\n\nCopy full SHA for 356bfd6 \n\n[ ](/samtools/htslib/blob/356bfd6b9a573afeed5e4e266f9e15ad71f10896/hts.c) [ ](/samtools/htslib/tree/356bfd6b9a573afeed5e4e266f9e15ad71f10896)\n\nMore actions \n\n  * ####  [ Make BAM zero-length intervals work like CRAM ](/samtools/htslib/commit/1c8c335d5c3a5a29edbe03b9d12338404aff8b48 \"Make BAM zero-length intervals work like CRAM\n\nFor a BED file with:\nchr1 1000 1000\n\nWorked with CRAM multi-region iterator but not with BAM.  This change makes them work the same.  Fixes #2060.\")\n\nShow description for 1c8c335 \n\n[ whitwham ](/samtools/htslib/commits?author=whitwham)\n\nauthored and \n\n[ daviesrob ](/samtools/htslib/commits?author=daviesrob)\n\ncommitted  on Jun 6, 2024 \n\n[ 1c8c335  ](/samtools/htslib/commit/1c8c335d5c3a5a29edbe03b9d12338404aff8b48)\n\nCopy full SHA for 1c8c335 \n\n[ ](/samtools/htslib/blob/1c8c335d5c3a5a29edbe03b9d12338404aff8b48/hts.c) [ ](/samtools/htslib/tree/1c8c335d5c3a5a29edbe03b9d12338404aff8b48)\n\nMore actions \n\n\n\n\n<::before>\n\n###  Commits on May 23, 2024 \n\n  * ####  [ Warn if bgzf_getline() returned apparently UTF-16-encoded text ](/samtools/htslib/commit/30c9c50a874059e3dae7ff8c0ad9e8a9258031c8 \"Warn if bgzf_getline\\(\\) returned apparently UTF-16-encoded text\n\nText files badly transferred from Windows may occasionally be\nUTF-16-encoded, and this may not be easily noticed by the user.\nHTSlib should not accept such encoding \\(as other tools surely don't,\nhence doing so would cause interoperability problems\\), but it should\nideally emit a warning or error message identifying the problem.\n\nReading text from a htsFile/samFile/vcfFile will already have failed\nwith EFTYPE/ENOEXEC if the text file is UTF-16-encoded, as the encoding\nwill not have been recognised by hts_detect_format\\(\\).\n\nOTOH bgzf_getline\\(\\) will return a UTF-16-encoded text line. Add a\nsuitable context-dependent diagnostic to the BGZF-based bgzf_getline\\(\\)\ncalls in HTSlib: in hts_readlist\\(\\)/hts_readlines\\(\\), emit a warning\n\\(once, on the first line\\); in tbx.c, emit a more specific error message\nif get_intv\\(\\) parsing failure is due to UTF-16 encoding.\n\n\\[TODO\\] If utf16_text_format were added to htsFormatCategory,\nthe new is_utf16_text\\(\\) function is suitable for detecting it.\")\n\nShow description for 30c9c50 \n\n[ jmarshall ](/samtools/htslib/commits?author=jmarshall)\n\nauthored and \n\n[ daviesrob ](/samtools/htslib/commits?author=daviesrob)\n\ncommitted  on May 23, 2024 \n\n[ 30c9c50  ](/samtools/htslib/commit/30c9c50a874059e3dae7ff8c0ad9e8a9258031c8)\n\nCopy full SHA for 30c9c50 \n\n[ ](/samtools/htslib/blob/30c9c50a874059e3dae7ff8c0ad9e8a9258031c8/hts.c) [ ](/samtools/htslib/tree/30c9c50a874059e3dae7ff8c0ad9e8a9258031c8)\n\nMore actions \n\n\n\n\n<::before>\n\n###  Commits on May 2, 2024 \n\n  * ####  [ Check interval start to avoid overflowing bin numbers ](/samtools/htslib/commit/9a99a1d574a0438d7f4e8a81e60b315f653f4b68 \"Check interval start to avoid overflowing bin numbers\n\nCheck start positions of query intervals against the maximum position\nrepresentable in the index's geometry, to avoid negative bin numbers\nand the resulting infinite loops in the do...while loop.\n\nIntroduce 